---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import { ENTITY, CONTACT } from '../lib/legal.js'

/* Scoped to what Prism is today: free, invite only, no payment, no company
   formed. Deliberately no arbitration clause, no venue and no choice of law —
   those need a lawyer and a legal entity, and a clause with a blank in it is
   worse than no clause. The longer draft lives in prism-aai/docs/legal. */
---

<Legal
  title="Terms — Prism"
  description="The terms for using Prism while it is free and invite only."
  heading="Terms"
>
  <p>
    Prism is free and invite only. These terms are short because the product is
    early and there is not much to argue about yet. They will get longer when
    there is.
  </p>

  <h2>What you get</h2>
  <p>
    An invite to use the Prism apps, at no charge, for as long as we keep the
    invite open. We can change what the product does, and we can stop offering
    it. If we are going to stop, we will give you notice and a way to get your
    notes out.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>
    One account, for you. Do not share your invite or your sign-in code. Tell us
    at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> if you think someone else is in
    your account.
  </p>

  <h2>Recording is on you</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>You are responsible for the legality of every recording you make.</strong>
    Prism records from your computer and does not announce itself to anyone
    else on the call. Recording law varies: some places need only your consent,
    some need everyone's. Knowing which one applies, and getting consent where
    it is needed, is your job and not ours.
  </p>
  <p>
    Do not use Prism to record people you are not allowed to record, to harass
    anyone, or to break the law where you are.
  </p>

  <h2>Your content is yours</h2>
  <p>
    Your recordings, transcripts and notes belong to you. We process them to
    provide the product, as described in <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>, and for
    nothing else. We do not train models on them and we do not sell them.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not promise</h2>
  <p>
    Transcription and note-writing are automated and imperfect. Accuracy drops
    with crosstalk, bad audio, and unfamiliar names. <strong>Do not rely on a Prism
    note as a record of a legally significant conversation without checking the
    transcript.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    The product is provided as it is, without warranties. It may be unavailable,
    it may lose a write-up, and it depends on third-party services we do not
    control. Keep your own copy of anything that matters.
  </p>

  <h2>Ending it</h2>
  <p>
    You can stop using Prism whenever you like; email
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a> to delete your account. We can end
    your access if you break these terms, and we will tell you why.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If these terms change materially we will date the change here and email
    account holders. {ENTITY} is early-stage and not yet incorporated; when that
    changes, the company behind the product will be named on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>
  </p>
</Legal>
